Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:49:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Privacy Settings (was writing to a dead table) and
 Download My Data (was calling a nonexistent endpoint)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Privacy Settings: the Profile > Privacy tab saved to a `user_privacy`
table (visibility, showOnline, showJoinedTrips, cityVisibility) that
nothing ever reads. The actual profile-viewing endpoint
(GET /api/users/:userId/profile) enforces a completely different set
of fields directly on `users` (profileVisibility, showEmail,
showPhone, showRealName, showBio, showLocation, showInterests,
showTravelHistory) that no UI ever set — so they sat at their
defaults forever. A user setting their profile to "Private" got a
success toast and zero actual protection.

Rewired GET/PATCH /api/me/privacy to read and write the fields that
are actually enforced, and rebuilt the Privacy tab around them.
Dropped "Friends Only" from the visibility options since it isn't
actually enforced differently from Public today (only 'private' is
checked) — offering it would just reintroduce the same problem.

Download My Data: the button called /api/user/download-data, which
doesn't exist, and even if it had, the handler never called
response.json() before stringifying — it would have downloaded a
near-empty file. There's already a real, working export endpoint at
GET /api/me/export; wired the button to that instead, fixed the
missing .json() parse, added chat messages and community questions
to the export (the button's own copy promised them but the export
didn't include them), and fixed lingering "Ceylon Expand" branding in
the exported filename and content.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
